From 3b38ccbb8980feca6f7bdd020f966e3fd15b2c40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:40:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 31/42] feat(scripting): layer texture animations, parents and
 children

ILayer had properties and no methods, so every call on a layer threw
"not a function". It now has:

- getTextureAnimation (): an ITextureAnimation over a sprite sheet or
  GIF texture (frameCount, duration, rate, play, pause, stop, join,
  isPlaying, getFrame, setFrame). A layer follows the shared render
  time until a script takes its animation over, then keeps its own
  position, rate and play state, as Wallpaper Engine does. The AM/PM
  sprite of 3299228616 cycled between both; its script pins the right
  one every frame (10530 log lines in 30 s before 0028).
- getParent () and getChildren (), for the layers scripts can reach
  (groups are not scriptable yet, so a group parent is undefined).

The animation clock is its own class with unit tests; the renderer
reads the layer's own texture from it.

